<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Labels for the personal build only.

  The public build is the canonical product and keeps the plain name, so a stranger installing it
  sees "Page Wallpaper" and nothing else. This copy is the exception, so this is the one that
  carries the qualifier.

  All three matter, because Android reads a different one in each place the app appears:
  app_name in the launcher, the share sheet and app settings; wallpaper_label in the live
  wallpaper picker; widget_label in the widget picker. Overriding one and not the others would
  leave two identically named entries in whichever list was missed — and the live wallpaper
  picker is the worst place to pick the wrong one.

  Only the strings are overridden. The icon is deliberately left alone: the text is enough to
  tell them apart, and a second icon would be work nobody has needed yet.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="app_name">Page Wallpaper (Personal)</string>
    <string name="wallpaper_label">Page Wallpaper (Personal)</string>
    <string name="widget_label">Page Wallpaper (Personal)</string>
</resources>
